  "summary_en": "UK statutory instrument implementing the EU Machinery Directive 2006/42/EC in Great Britain (as amended post-Brexit). It requires machinery to be safe, meet essential health and safety requirements, undergo conformity assessment, carry UK marking, and sets approved-body designation, enforcement and penalties. Relevant to robots only as machinery; no AI provisions.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Responsible persons must not place machinery on the market unless it is safe and meets essential health and safety requirements",
   "Conformity assessment procedures, technical file, declaration of conformity and UK marking are required",
   "Machinery built to designated standards is presumed compliant",
   "Secretary of State designates and monitors approved bodies",
   "Offences carry fines and up to two years' imprisonment; due diligence defence available"
  ],
